                <pb facs="0210" n="108" xml:id="pg108"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 774/393.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Vignaud to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-11-04"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November 4, 1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 528.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that Mr. Pichon
                    has just notified this embassy of the appointment of the three French delegates
                    to the opium conference. They are: M. L. O. Ratard, consul general of France at
                    Shanghai; Mr. Brenier, under director of the department of agriculture, forests,
                    and commerce of Indo-China; and M. Cronillon, inspector of first grade of the
                    customhouse service of Indo-China.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Vignaud.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
